    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="0773" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.3727/11–2246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-11-22T19:00:00-05:00">November 22, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>730. CAB and Dept now consider it desirable to explore question holding
                    discussions on bilateral air agreement in near future. Earliest possible date
                    around first of year due to Canadian talks here. Embs <pb facs="0774" n="756"
                        xml:id="pg756"/> opinion on timing desired in view of Desp 2205 of September
                        24.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d661-f1"/> Howard’s travel to Washington for
                    consultation being requested prior his return Habana.<anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d661-f2"/> Emb will be advised.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d661-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d661-f1" n="80" xml:id="d661-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 60, <ref target="#pg743">p. 743</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d661-f2" n="81" xml:id="d661-f2-content">
                <p>The Commercial Attaché (Howard) was on vacation in Florida.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d661-f3" n="82" xml:id="d661-f3-content">
                <p>The Embassy was instructed in airgram 1440, December 6, 1946, to ask the Cuban
                    Government officially whether it was agreeable to the opening of negotiations
                    shortly after the first of the year (711.3727/11–2746).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
